validating (merge window), validation_failed (parked). pr_approved is deliberately NOT excluded: the sticky approval is exactly why REWORK is the right leg — after the rework push, validate-armed re-validates the new head and merge proceeds without a re-review (rework re-validates, never re-reviews); review-threads-resolved keeps excluding pr_approved so no review stacks on top. prMachineAuthor fails closed (owner rule: auto-rework is machine-only, same as fail_validation/conflict-rework). localAction arm_rework labels the PR agent:rework + explains in a comment; rework-on-label dispatches the leg (issue-anchored, PR-anchored fallback #544) and consumes the label. gh-807 ARMING-SIDE STICKY APPROVAL: before arming, the action reads the machine verdict records (js/common/reviewVerdicts.js) for the CURRENT head — an APPROVE verdict with zero BLOCKING findings withholds the arm (suggestions do not trigger rework; the approval is authoritative and the PR must not re-enter the rework loop next to its sticky pr_approved); APPROVE with blocking>0 or a REQUEST_CHANGES/BLOCK verdict arms as before. Fails open on PRs without records (pre-gh-807). The three conflict-shaped reconcile-review-verdicts rules (above — reconcile-rework-vs-approval / reconcile-issue-rework-vs-approval / reconcile-approval-vs-changes) de-conflict the labels in the same tick, and an APPROVE head keeps any CI-driven rework arm (the reconcile action's headHasRealFailure exemption). gh-957 NO-OP LOOP GUARD: the arm (and the gh-840 restore sweep) is WITHHELD once noopLapMax (default 2) consecutive rework laps on the SAME head closed with ZERO pushed commits AND ZERO resolved threads — the lap markers the rework post-action stamps are the audit; escalation is one label (rework-loop-escalated) + owner comment per head. A lap that pushed or resolved anything, or a new head, resets the budget. The rework leg input is GraphQL-sourced (the same reviewThreads census this rule counts) and a leg that replies to ever